		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=3930&amp;p=30701#p30701"><![CDATA[
Making a recording probably wouldn't help. The tones won't be recorded. <br><br>It is not unusual for CTCSS to sometimes be affected by individual voices.  The transmitting radio should filter out any low frequencies in the voice before adding the CTCSS tone and likewise the receiving radio should filter out any voice frequencies to leave the CTCSS tone, but this filtering is not perfect and sometimes voice tones will interfere with the CTCSS decoding. <br><br>High modulation levels will also introduce distortion or noise to the signal which again can cause problems. <br><br>Colin G4EML<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=87">G4EML</a> — Mon Apr 08, 2024 10:36 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
